1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,345
Water, spraying out of a frozen moon,

2
00:00:03,345 --> 00:00:04,250
into space.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,150
This is the real image.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,247
A moon barely five hundred kilometres across,

5
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:14,625
leaking an ocean.

6
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:18,329
In 2015 came the verdict:

7
00:00:18,329 --> 00:00:19,681
a global ocean,

8
00:00:19,681 --> 00:00:22,475
wrapped around the entire moon.

9
00:00:23,925 --> 00:00:26,805
Cassini flew straight through the plume and

10
00:00:26,805 --> 00:00:27,475
tasted it.

11
00:00:28,925 --> 00:00:30,456
It found hydrogen.

12
00:00:30,456 --> 00:00:31,903
And for microbes,

13
00:00:31,903 --> 00:00:32,839
it is food:

14
00:00:32,839 --> 00:00:34,200
chemical energy.

15
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:37,752
Water. Energy. Chemistry.

16
00:00:37,752 --> 00:00:40,275
Every box we know how to tick.

17
00:00:41,725 --> 00:00:44,459
So, is something alive in the ocean

18
00:00:44,459 --> 00:00:45,475
of Enceladus?

19
00:00:46,925 --> 00:00:49,425
Nobody knows. Not yet.
